        "bhavartha": "The verse lines up what Śiva is: unborn and eternal, the cause behind causes, auspicious and alone, the one who makes the lights themselves shine. He is the Fourth, beyond the darkness of ignorance, with no beginning and no end. In this Supreme One, who makes pure and in whom there is no 'two', the poet takes refuge."
